 {"chainIds":[143],"lens":"L1",
  "check":"Monad v0.16.5, and v0.16.7 which rpc.monad.xyz now reports: can the varcode cache (interpreter code and native code keyed by code hash) store or find analysis or machine code of one bytecode under the PoolManager's code hash, for a 7702-delegated account or for an account created and called in the same block under optimistic parallel execution (lead L-647).",
  "result":"No. Monad never pairs a code hash with code read separately. execute_call_message reads the hash with state.get_code_hash(msg.code_address) and then fetches the code by that hash, state.read_code(hash), and passes both to the VM (category/execution/ethereum/execute_message.cpp lines 326-330). For a delegated account the delegate address is read first (category/vm/evm/delegation.cpp lines 57-80) and the hash and code are then those of the delegate, the code again fetched by hash. read_code looks up the transaction's own code map, then BlockState, then the code trie, each keyed by hash (state3/state.cpp lines 523-532, state2/block_state.cpp lines 129-153). Every entry of those stores has a key computed from its bytes: State::set_code computes keccak256(code) (state3/state.cpp lines 576-587), BlockState::merge copies a transaction's code map entries under the same hashes (block_state.cpp lines 194-216), and the RPC state override goes through set_code (category/rpc/monad_executor.cpp line 171). VarcodeCache::try_set_raw returns an existing entry for a hash without comparing bytes (category/vm/varcode_cache.cpp lines 74-82), which is safe only because of that invariant, and the invariant holds on every insert path read. Under optimistic execution a transaction that read an account before an earlier transaction changed its code fails can_merge, which compares the recorded code_hash (state3/state.cpp lines 664-666), and runs again. Compiled code is keyed by the same hash and recompiled when the chain revision changes (category/vm/vm.cpp lines 142-160). state.cpp, varcode_cache.cpp, vm.cpp and delegation.cpp are byte-identical in v0.16.7, and the v0.16.7 changes to execute_message.cpp and block_state.cpp touch only the ripemd touch and include comments.",
  "source": MON + "category/execution/ethereum/execute_message.cpp lines 326-330; also " + MON + "category/execution/ethereum/state3/state.cpp lines 523-587, 664-666, " + MON + "category/execution/ethereum/state2/block_state.cpp lines 129-216, " + MON + "category/vm/varcode_cache.cpp lines 41-82, " + MON + "category/vm/evm/delegation.cpp lines 57-80, " + MON7 + " (same files)"},
